> > to botpi si velvelzilbotpi toi
> > 
> ki'A.  Having erased {botpi} we are left with a predicate whose first 
> argument is the fourth place of an argument whose fourth place has been 
> deleted and which did not have a fifth place to move up.  So what was the 
> intended message?

Yuck. That's right. I wanted to talk about a Klein bottle and started saying
{lo la klain. botpi}, but then I realized that a Klein bottle is not a botpi
since it can never have a cap. So I used one of the place-switching-around
methods in the Book's lujvo chapter, assuming it would work the same way for
zi'o.

I now see that because zi'o actually eradicates the place it is not necessary
to switch it back, so it is simply a {zilvelbotpi}.
